  "Question": "If \\(y=(m-2)x^2+3x-1\\) is a quadratic function, what condition must \\(m\\) satisfy? Which of the following is correct?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(m=2\\)",
    "B": "\\(m\\ne2\\)",
    "C": "\\(m>2\\)",
    "D": "\\(m\\ne0\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "A quadratic function requires the coefficient of the quadratic term to be nonzero, so \\(m-2\\ne0\\). Therefore, \\(m\\ne2\\).",
